{{fbdoc item="title" value="Sound Library Reference"}}----
Procedures and command families for FreeBASIC's built-in sound library.

{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	The sound library, or ##sfxlib##, provides generated tones, PLAY-string music, music file playback, sample playback, MIDI control, audio device selection, and capture support.  Programs that use these commands link the sound library automatically.
	
	If a program intentionally does not use the sound command surface and needs selected sfxlib command words as normal identifiers, define ##[[KeyPgFbNoSfxlib|FB_NO_SFXLIB]]## before those names are parsed.

**{{anchor name="GENERATED|Generated Sound"}}**
	Commands for tones, notes, PLAY strings, generated waveforms, and mix state.
**{{anchor name="MEDIA|Digital Audio and MIDI"}}**
	Commands for music files, loaded samples, and MIDI.
**{{anchor name="DEVICE|Devices and Capture"}}**
	Commands for selecting output drivers and recording input.

<<{{anchor name="GENERATED"}}{{fbdoc item="section" value="Generated Sound"}}
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgBeep|BEEP"}}==
		Produces a beep or a short pitched note.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|Generated sound commands"}}==
		Documents ##SOUND##, ##TONE##, ##NOISE##, ##NOTE##, ##PLAY##, ##TEMPO##, ##CHANNEL##, ##OCTAVE##, ##VOICE##, ##VOL##, ##VOLUME##, ##BALANCE##, ##PAN##, ##WAVE##, ##ENVELOPE##, and ##INSTRUMENT##.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|SOUND"}}==
		Plays a generated tone.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|TONE"}}==
		Plays a generated tone on a channel.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|NOISE"}}==
		Plays generated noise on a channel.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|NOTE"}}==
		Plays a named note.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|PLAY"}}==
		Plays BASIC PLAY strings.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|TEMPO"}}==
		Sets or returns the generated-sound tempo.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|CHANNEL"}}==
		Sets or returns the generated-sound channel.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|OCTAVE"}}==
		Sets or returns the default note octave.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|VOICE"}}==
		Sets or returns the default instrument.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|VOL"}}==
		Sets the master volume.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|VOLUME"}}==
		Sets or returns master or channel volume.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|BALANCE"}}==
		Sets or returns the master stereo balance.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|PAN"}}==
		Sets or returns channel stereo pan.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|WAVE"}}==
		Defines a generated waveform.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|ENVELOPE"}}==
		Defines an ADSR envelope.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxGenerated|INSTRUMENT"}}==
		Defines or assigns an instrument.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Digital Audio and MIDI"}}
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgMusic|MUSIC"}}==
		Loads, plays, loops, pauses, resumes, stops, and queries music assets.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfx|SFX"}}==
		Loads and controls short sound effects by id or channel.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgMidi|MIDI"}}==
		Opens MIDI output, plays MIDI files, and sends MIDI messages.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Devices and Capture"}}
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgDevice|DEVICE"}}==
		Lists, selects, and queries sfxlib output devices.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgCapture|CAPTURE"}}==
		Starts, pauses, resumes, stops, reads, and saves audio capture.
>>::c::

